  "description": "Input authority must not activate before REPLAY_DONE (immortality §6.3): keystrokes typed while the screen is still replaying are how you type into the wrong prompt on a production router. The worker accepts input on a data peer only after it has sent replay_done; an input frame before it — here the core's input 3, a core defect, since the core sends input only after live — is not delivered and is answered input_refused replaying, never silently dropped. Captures of a correct core show none.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §6.3",
    "decision 5.38"
  ],
